  "body": "## The defect\n\nThe meet law of the Rotary Flow kernel read only adjacent guide pairs. The call is in the band loop of `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary_flow.rs`. A guide that crossed a guide that is not its neighbour in the pick was not checked. The kernel machined the set, and the bands of the two adjacent pairs folded through the same ground. No diagnostic said so (#4032, found in the safety-tier review of PR #4018).\n\n## The law\n\n- A new module, `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary_flow_cross.rs`, holds `refuse_crossed_set`.\n- It reads each pair of guides `i < j` with `j >= i + 2`, over the complete set.\n- It runs once, after the set normalization and before the first band is cut. No pass is generated for a refused set.\n- The exact test is the existing Ericson 5.1 segment-pair solve (`rotary_flow_set::seg_seg_at`, now `pub(super)`), with the same corner-lattice dust as the adjacent law.\n- An axis-aligned box prefilter, padded by the dust, skips each chain pair and each segment pair that cannot come within the dust. A NaN box reads as \"near\", so the exact solve decides.\n- The refusal names the two guides and the crossing point, in the text and as the error location:\n  `Rotary Flow: guide chains 1 and 3 meet or cross each other at (8.000, 0.000, 2.000), segment 1 of chain 1 - ...`\n- The adjacent pairs keep their own law in the band loop. That code and its refusal order did not change.\n- `rotary_flow.rs` lost a duplicate doc paragraph, so the file grows by 2 lines only (419 -> 421). `rotary_flow_set.rs` (459 lines) did not grow.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The #4032 reproduction (R8 prism, 72 sides, Z0..Z32, guide 3 down to `(0, 2)` and back) is refused by name at `(8, 0, 2)`.\n- A clean three-guide set on the same prism machines, and the notes state the shared boundary.\n- The existing Rotary Flow tests are unchanged and pass. No golden moved.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` lib, `multiaxis::rotary_flow_cross::tests`:\n  - `a_crossing_between_non_adjacent_chains_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `overlapping_boxes_without_a_crossing_pass`\n  - `far_boxes_skip_the_pair_and_a_nan_box_reads_near`\n- `camcraft-motion` suite `rotary_flow` (`tests/rotary_flow/bands.rs`, an existing directory suite):\n  - `a_crossing_between_non_adjacent_guides_is_refused_by_name` (the issue's reproduction)\n  - `a_clean_three_guide_set_on_the_prism_still_machines`\n\n## Mutation\n\nThe mutation limits the new law to adjacent pairs again (`for j in (i + 2)..chains.len()` becomes `for j in (i + 1)..(i + 2).min(chains.len())`). Run on winbuild at head `c3f531381`, log `C:\\camcraft-logs\\mut-4032-c3f531381.log`:\n\n- `a_crossing_between_non_adjacent_chains_is_refused_by_name`: RED (panic at `rotary_flow_cross.rs:135`, the `unwrap_err`).\n- `a_crossing_between_non_adjacent_guides_is_refused_by_name`: RED (panic at `bands.rs:192`, the kernel machined the set).\n- `overlapping_boxes_without_a_crossing_pass`: also RED (its adjacent-meet assertion), as expected.\n\nThe file was restored after the run (`git status` clean).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Gate (Windows, winbuild)\n\nAll runs are on Windows (winbuild), on head `c3f531381790e15cd3db608e3efc514fedbdad3b`. `origin/main` was `12ea01a45`, the base of the branch, so the trial merge was a no-op. Environment: `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_STALL_MIN=45`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: `wall 11.7 min, 41 step(s), 0 failed, 0 stalled`, `GATE_EXIT=0`. The log `C:\\camcraft-logs\\gate-4032-c3f531381.log` has the head SHA on line 1. The plan holds the motion lib, the `rotary_flow` suite (the new pins), 20 other motion suites, and 18 app suites, among them `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `example_catalog*` by name, again: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog --test example_catalog_adaptive --test example_catalog_edge_work`: 43 + 1 + 1 passed, `CATALOG_EXIT=0`.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: `6 step(s), 0 failed, 0 stalled`, `LIGHT_EXIT=0`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean, `CLIPPY_EXIT=0`. The app crate did not change.\n- No heavy step (P3).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes (P3: no heavy step, by \"Heavy lanes at review\").\n- macOS and Linux builds of this head. The gate ran on Windows only.\n- The app-level Rotary Flow suites outside the quick plan, except the example catalog suites named above.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/4032-rotary-flow-crossing.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Rotary Flow now refuses a guide set where any two guide chains meet or cross, not only adjacent ones. The refusal names the two guides and the crossing point.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4032\n",
